# ChanoX2 Architecture & UI Rules

## 1. Brand & Design System Consistency (ChanomHub Standard)
- All pages (Store/Home, Library, Downloads, Settings, ArticleDetail) and global shell components (TitleBar, MenuBar) must share the **same visual language** and **Warm Dark Amber** palette.
- **NEVER** use old Steam blue hardcoded colors (`#66c0f4`, `#1b2838`, `#1a2a3a`, `#2d3a4f`) or arbitrary hex colors (`#0a0e14`, `#111721`).
- **NEVER** mix conflicting accent colors across pages (e.g. `rose-500` in Home vs cyan elsewhere).
- **ALWAYS** use semantic Tailwind tokens:
  - Page background: `bg-background`
  - Cards & panels: `bg-card`
  - Secondary/muted panels: `bg-muted`
  - Primary text: `text-foreground`
  - Supporting text: `text-muted-foreground`
  - Borders & dividers: `border-border`
  - Primary interactive CTA / Active tabs: `bg-primary`, `text-primary`, `border-primary`
  - Destructive actions: `text-destructive`, `bg-destructive`

## 2. Component Guidelines
- Use UI primitives from `@/components/ui` (`Button`, `Card`, `Dialog`, `Input`, `Badge`).
- Use icons strictly from `lucide-react`.
- Border radius must remain consistent: `rounded-lg` for controls/inputs, `rounded-xl` for cards/dialogs.
